#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# sec

#% text
# `sec(x)` gives the secant 1/cos(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `sec(x)` stays unevaluated for symbolic `x`; where `cos(x)` has an exact value, `sec(x)` is its reciprocal.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% item
# `sec` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
sec(pi/3)
#% output
#= 2

#% cell
sec(1.0)
#% output
#= 1.8508157176809255

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Symbolic arguments and symmetry:

#% cell
sec(-x)
#% output
#= sec(x)

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(sec(1), 30)
#% output
#= 1.8508157176809256179117532413986502

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `cos`, `sin`, `cos`, `tan`
